From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Windows 11's window frame and caption buttons

The approved Windows 11 prototype (PS5_Proton-design prototypes/windows11-shell) draws a window as Windows 11 does:
a 1-pixel border round a 32-pixel title bar and the client, the caption buttons 46 x 32 side by side in the bar's
top right corner with no plate at rest, lit while the pointer is over them. Wine drew the classic frame (a raised
edge and the sizing border, 4 pixels), buttons inset by 2 pixels with 1-pixel gaps, a line under the caption, and
never a hot button. With the managed theme's bitmaps (PS5_Proton tools/pw_caption_buttons.py, measured from the
prototype) this draws the same pixels:

- A framed top-level window's visible rect is its window rect less the invisible part of the frame (all of it but the
  innermost pixel; all of it when maximized), as DWM shows Windows 11 windows, for a driver that decorates nothing
  (get_visible_rect). The frame still sizes the window: the server's hit test keeps the window rect for top-level
  windows. The visible pixel is the caption's colour; the PS5 compositor draws Windows 11's default border over it
  (the server's default border, #66757575).
- The caption buttons are SM_CXSIZE wide and SM_CYCAPTION tall from the inside rect's top right, close first; hit
  testing uses the same rectangles. The caption bar fills SM_CYCAPTION with no line beneath it; the icon and the
  title each start 16 pixels after what precedes them.
- DWMWA_EXTENDED_FRAME_BOUNDS answers those visible bounds, as on Windows 11 (it answered GetWindowRect).
- WM_NCMOUSEMOVE over a button draws it hot (CBS_HOT, passed to the theme hook as down = 2, which the classic
  fallback draws DFCS_HOT) and tracks the non-client leave; moving off it or WM_NCMOUSELEAVE draws it normal again.
  A repaint keeps the hot button.
---
diff --git a/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c b/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c
index 2518fce..ec14bf9 100644
--- a/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c
+++ b/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c
@@ -277,7 +277,35 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DwmGetWindowAttribute(HWND hwnd, DWORD attribute, PVOID pv_attrib
         /* DWM frame bounds are always in physical coords */
         context = SetThreadDpiAwarenessContext(DPI_AWARENESS_CONTEXT_PER_MONITOR_AWARE);
         if (GetWindowRect(hwnd, rect))
+        {
+            /* What the window shows: inside the invisible part of its resize border, as win32u's visible rect keeps
+             * it (PS5_Proton patch 1136, get_visible_rect and get_dwm_frame_inset): a 1-pixel border, none maximized. */
+            DWORD style = GetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE), ex_style = GetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE);
+            RECT client;
+            POINT origin = {0, 0};
+            int x = 0, y = 0;
+
+            if ((style & WS_THICKFRAME) && (style & (WS_DLGFRAME | WS_BORDER)) != WS_DLGFRAME)
+            {
+                x = GetSystemMetrics(SM_CXFRAME);
+                y = GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYFRAME);
+            }
+            else if ((ex_style & WS_EX_DLGMODALFRAME) || ((style & WS_DLGFRAME) && !(style & WS_THICKFRAME)))
+            {
+                x = GetSystemMetrics(SM_CXDLGFRAME);
+                y = GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYDLGFRAME);
+            }
+            if (x && !(style & WS_MAXIMIZE))
+            {
+                x -= GetSystemMetrics(SM_CXBORDER);
+                y -= GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYBORDER);
+            }
+            GetClientRect(hwnd, &client);
+            ClientToScreen(hwnd, &origin);
+            OffsetRect(&client, origin.x, origin.y);
+            if (!EqualRect(&client, rect) && GetWindowRgnBox(hwnd, &client) == ERROR) InflateRect(rect, -x, -y);
             hr = S_OK;
+        }
         else
             hr = HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(GetLastError());
 
